Design a synchronous circuit that generates a 4-bit Gray code sequence. The output `gray_out` updates on each positive edge of the clock signal `clk`, and will reset to `0000` when the reset signal `rst` is asserted. The module uses a state machine approach where the output transitions through predefined Gray code values in a specific order, offering an efficient method of transitioning between values to minimize errors in digital systems where only one bit changes at a time.
