Design a Read-Only Memory (ROM) module capable of storing 16 words, each 8 bits wide. The module has a 4-bit address input that allows for addressing any of the 16 memory locations. It outputs two bits of data simultaneously, with out[0] carrying the least significant byte and out[1] theoretically intended to carry the next significant byte, although they are using the same 8-bit memory output in this case. The module initializes its memory with predefined values upon instantiation, making it suitable for applications requiring static data storage like firmware or constants.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] addr,
  output [m-1:0] out
);

