description:
Design a front-edge detector that identifies the transition from LOW to HIGH on an input signal (`sig_in`) and produces a HIGH output (`sig_out`) for one clock cycle while delaying to ensure the output is cleanly registered. The module utilizes a 3-bit delay counter that resets upon detecting the rising edge, ensuring that `sig_out` is set HIGH only when the delay reaches a specific count. The design effectively debounces the input signal to prevent false triggering from noise or glitches.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input sig_in,
    output sig_out
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input sig_in,
    output sig_out
    );reg [2:0] delay = 'd7;

assign sig_out = (delay == 'd6)? 1'd1: 1'd0;

reg [1:0] trig = 'd0;
always@(posedge clk)
begin
	trig <= {trig[0],sig_in};
end

wire start = (trig == 2'b01) ? 1'b1 : 1'b0; 

always@(posedge clk)
begin
	if (start == 1'd1) delay<= 'd0;
	if (delay < 'd7) delay <= delay + 'd1;
end

endmodule

