description:
Design a 4-bit refresh counter that increments its value on the rising edge of the `refreshClk` signal. The counter resets to zero when it reaches a value of 8 (i.e., when it is greater than or equal to 7). This module is typically used to generate periodic signals or control refresh operations in applications such as display refresh mechanisms.
module top_module(
    input wire refreshClk,
    output reg [3:0] refreshCounter = 0
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input wire refreshClk,
    output reg [3:0] refreshCounter = 0
    );always @(posedge refreshClk)
    begin
        refreshCounter <= refreshCounter + 1;
        if(refreshCounter >= 7)
            refreshCounter <= 0;
    end

endmodule

